==Evolution==
Evolves into '''CAT-6 Siege Engine''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''CAT-8 Behemoth''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''CAT-10 Gigapult''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Mighty Kat-A-Pult is a similar tanker to [[Sea Maiden Ruri (Uber Rare Cat)|Sea Maiden Ruri]]. The crew has incredible health against their target, but their usage is bogged down in several aspects, primarily their extremely long cooldown for a tank, their blindspot and low damage. These problems are further exacerbated in their niche, as zombies are generally low-ranged pushers and it does not have any offensive abilities to deal with ranged threats. More often than not, your other anti-zombie specialists would be doing most of the work. With that being said though, they can still be useful sometimes, due to their good ability to soak up zombie damage, ability to provide a pretty good weaken when it hits, and offer decent support against foes that can be annoying and enemy peons. Additionally, if a Zombie [[Burrow]]s or [[Revive]]s onto them, they can use that Zombie enemy as a stepping stone to attack and Weaken other Zombies. Although they may not be as good as [[Mighty Thermae D-Lux (Uber Rare Cat)|Subterra Guardians]] or other Ubers in their set, they can still help sometimes and provide use in certain cases.

==='''True Form'''===
The standing range and AOE increase do make them better by reducing their blindspot and making them less vulnerable to enemy rangers. However, these do not change much about this unit's overall performance as a generalist or specialist.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
CAT-10 Gigapult is a massive improvement to this unit, not only improving its usage against Zombies, but also giving it [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] targeting. Since CAT-10 Gigapult was a unit that was heavily reliant on stats, boosting them to level 60 gives them ridiculous amounts of health against targeted traits. Having over one million effective health without weaken, and far surpassing two million with it. Their weaken ability is also of extremely good quality, as it now has both 100% proc chance and very close to 100% uptime against both traits. (The uptime against Relics is only seven hundredths of a second away from being 100%)

CAT-10 Gigapult also possesses some of the craziest LD in the game, having tons of piercing range while basically having no blindspot at all. Even Doge variants cannot enter this blindspot without speed clipping, which goes to show how insignificant it is. The only time their blindspot may be a problem is if a burrowing zombie gets inside of it, and even then CAT-10 Gigapult can easily tank hits with their millions of health against Zombies. This also improves their weaken ability, as they are now able to nearly permanently weaken an entire field of Relics and Zombies.

Lastly, CAT-10 Gigapult gained a DPS increase of around 60%. This is the biggest improvement that this unit received in Ultra Form by far, as it is now one of the best generalists in the game. While 10k DPS isn't a crazy number in comparison to other level 60 ubers, their insanely wide LD makes it so that this DPS is applied to basically the entire field. This is something that no other uber can replicate, as ubers with CAT-10 Gigapult's level of piercing range usually come with a big blindspot, with prime examples being [[Sea Serpent Daliasan (Uber Rare Cat)|Daliasan]] and [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Aphrodite]]. Their general usage is truly ridiculous. They have great DPS, amazing piercing range, almost no blindspot, and also very high health. The only stats that CAT-10 Gigapult are truly lacking in is cost and cooldown, although this is pretty much entirely insignificant due to how much value you can get by simply sending one CAT-10 Gigapult out on the field.

CAT-10 Gigapult also gains Curse and Toxic Immune. Curse is essential for an Anti-Relic and is a great improvement to this unit, while toxic simply makes CAT-10 Gigapult better against enemies that happen to possess that ability, with [[Zollow]] and [[Big Peng Z]] being prime examples.

==='''Talents'''===
All of this unit's talents are fairly mediocre for their extreme cost. Stat talents are obviously helpful given their ability to tank zombies and hit threats at range, but they don't do much more, even with [[Catseye]]s and [[Ultra Form]].

Wave Attacks allow the unit to snipe enemies beyond its maximum effective range and can cover their blindspot. But be mindful, the unit's slow attack rate and 20% activation chance means it'll be difficult for them to get the most out of it. With the Ultra Form all but removing the blindspot, this is mostly used for the extra DPS. However, given its already high damage, it is highly likely to already knock back or kill enemies on hit, making wave attacks fairly irrelevant for most peons, and less tanky enemy units such as [[Zory]], [[Zang Roo]], [[Sir Rel]], ETC. This is also the case for enemies with exceptionally high knockback counts, like [[Mr. Puffington]], or [[M. Ost]] to a lesser degree. While sometimes useful, it is not worthwhile enough for its NP Cost.

Slow is rather situational due to the existence of [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]]'s Target Zombie talent and [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]]'s target Relic and how it's often used against melee-ranged zombies/relics, which this unit has trouble dealing with without the assistance of [[Ultra Form]]. Additionally, most relevant Zombie enemies simply die, or burrow too quickly for this effect to be overwhelmingly useful. This is not to say it doesn't have its use cases, as it can prevent [[Miss Haka]] from burrowing, or stall [[Oldhorn]]; but just like its Wave attacks, this is situational at best and not worth your NP.

Similarly, Resist Freeze is not all that useful, even within its niche, as the few threats that employ them are better dealt with other means of destruction.

==='''Orb'''===
Resistance against Zombie/Relic Orb for better tanking or Berserker ability orb for damage due Long Distance.

